    "title": "Letters: Personal privacy has already been missing for many years - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Howard Harrison ,\n8 hours ago The more help we can provide our police department, the better our city will become.\nThere are to many “wackos” running around who do not give one thought about your privacy.\nPerhaps if those who are flapping their jaws about privacy being invaded would take a look around they would see that their privacy went down the road many years ago. Example: Give someone your telephone number, and they will tell you what you had for breakfast.\nAdd those cameras!",
